# Explanation

- The constructor of the `Logger` class is declared **private**, preventing direct object creation.
- The static method `getInstance()` creates the object only once.
- Every subsequent call to `getInstance()` returns the same object.
- This guarantees that only one instance of the `Logger` class exists throughout the application.

